    <item>
      <title>CORRECT: India’s Quick-Commerce Architect Eyes Long Bets</title>
      <link>https://www.bloomberg.com/news/videos/2026-09-17/india-s-quick-commerce-architect-takes-on-slow-wagers-video</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">8d1e6b356f55cf30fe2b0a67</guid>
      <pubDate>Thu, 17 Sep 2026 23:06:26 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>The man who transformed how urban India eats, dines, and shops, Deepinder Goyal built his food delivery startup Zomato into one of the country’s biggest consumer technology companies, Eternal. At the height of its success, Goyal stepped away from the day-to-day running of the company he built, to turn his attention to a very different set of challenges with a much longer horizon.

In an exclusive interview on his sprawling residence in Delhi, Bloomberg’s Haslinda Amin speaks with Goyal about the never-ending journeys of founders, his current pursuits, and his quest for a different kind of eternity.

Correct: Video updated to correct currency in stock price charts at 04:12 and 07:50 of the program. (Source: Bloomberg)</description>
